concepts":["gamification","prediction markets","system design","leaderboard logic","user-AI interaction"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Users compete against AI in direct prediction duels","Winner-takes-all mechanic for staked crystals","Ambiguity regarding the \"betting ticket\" feature and its reward structure","Leaderboard ranking criteria under development"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvlypys_1ac1cfa585d9","importance":8,"narrative":"The user initiated a design discussion for the prediction system, focusing on gamifying the interaction between users and the AI. We need to define clear metrics for the AI's prediction accuracy and determine a compelling reward mechanism for the ticket-based betting mode to ensure user engagement.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Conceptualizing the prediction engine, user-AI duels, and leaderboard logic","timestamp":"2026-06-01T19:35:11.821Z","title":"System Design: AI Prediction and Betting Mechanics","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvm7nvz_7968bd980304":{"concepts":["gamification","betting logic","scoring engine","UX design"],"confidence":1,"facts":["User selected \"Duel vs AI\" as the initial mode after scoring motor implementation.","Complexity level set to \"Complet: toate 5 piețele\" (1X2, exact score, over/under, BTTS, first scorer).","Requirement to display AI predictions before the duel to allow users to counter-bet.","Clarification requested on the game design philosophy regarding users betting against AI predictions."],"files":["pred_challenges"],"id":"obs_mpvm7nvz_7968bd980304","importance":8,"narrative":"The product direction is finalized towards a 1v1 duel mode against the AI, utilizing a multi-market scoring system. The user specifically requested transparency in AI predictions prior to the user's move, despite concerns about how this influences the competitive mechanic.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Duel mode vs AI defined with 5-market complexity","timestamp":"2026-06-01T19:42:09.043Z","title":"Product requirements for scoring motor and user modes","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvmiuyt_1334edd6a427":{"concepts":["UX design","gamification","progressive disclosure","user engagement"],"confidence":1,"facts":["User proposed a \"reveal\" mechanic where only 1X2 result is shown initially.","Remaining predictions (Exact Score, Over/Under, etc.) should be hidden until the user submits their own prediction.","The strategy applies to both the general listing and individual match detail pages.","User expresses uncertainty about whether hiding all data is the best approach for UX."],"files":["src/components/predictions/MatchPredictionCard.tsx"],"id":"obs_mpvmiuyt_1334edd6a427","importance":6,"narrative":"The user wants to gamify the prediction interface by introducing a reveal mechanism to encourage user interaction. By gating detailed prediction stats (Score, Over/Under) until after the user submits their own choice, we increase engagement and reduce data overload. The challenge is balancing this restrictive UI pattern with the need to eventually display full match analysis.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Refining user engagement by gating detailed prediction data","timestamp":"2026-06-01T19:50:51.433Z","title":"UI/UX Strategy for Prediction Display","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvmqp9p_3df39080f51e":{"concepts":["UI/UX redesign","Conditional rendering","Access control logic","Gamification"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Prediction visibility gated by user submission requirement.","All predictions become public after the associated match starts.","Frontend needs styling improvements for the predictions section."],"files":["frontend/src/components/Predictions.js","frontend/src/styles/predictions.css"],"id":"obs_mpvmqp9p_3df39080f51e","importance":6,"narrative":"The user requested a UI/UX overhaul for the prediction interface and a shift in business logic regarding prediction visibility. Predictions are now hidden until a