pt relies on a sequence of internal API calls to update match states and trigger client-side refreshes.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Reviewing update-5min.sh execution flow","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:32:53.013Z","title":"Read cron script task sequence","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvq6bv9_b661f470ada4":{"concepts":["cron automation","idempotent API endpoints","data pipeline","shell scripting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Inserted '/api/challenges/resolve' POST request after 'live-matches' sync.","Added dynamic parsing of the 'resolved' count from the API response.","Updated step counter in log messages (from 6 steps to 7)."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/update-5min.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvq6bv9_b661f470ada4","importance":5,"narrative":"The cron job script was updated to automatically resolve AI-managed duels immediately after syncing match statuses. This ensures that when a match finishes, any associated duels are processed without waiting for the next full refresh cycle.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Adding post-sync match resolution to the data pipeline","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:33:05.274Z","title":"Update 5-minute cron script with AI duel resolution step","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvq6glo_b75e1ebe637e":{"concepts":["API testing","curl","local development server"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Target endpoint: http://localhost:4321/api/challenges/resolve","Response status: success: true","Current state: resolved: 0, skipped: 0, matches: 0"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvq6glo_b75e1ebe637e","importance":4,"narrative":"Verified the connectivity and basic functionality of the challenge resolution API. The endpoint is operational and returns a successful response, although no challenges were processed in this initial call.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"curl request to localhost:4321","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:33:11.411Z","title":"Test API challenge resolve endpoint","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvqrke7_80436e3dbb00":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","job scheduling","process consolidation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Decision made to implement a unified tick.sh script running every 30 seconds.","The orchestrator will handle multiple cadences: live (30s), resolve (1min), refresh (5min), and ai:predict (daily).","This replaces existing separate cron scripts and includes a refactor of the current live cron."],"files":["tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvqrke7_80436e3dbb00","importance":7,"narrative":"We decided to unify cron job management into a single orchestrator script rather than maintaining fragmented processes. This approach ensures consistent execution cycles for all background tasks, including the previously neglected daily AI prediction job.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Consolidating disparate cron scripts into a single orchestrator","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:49:36.099Z","title":"Cron Orchestration Strategy Selection","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvqsryz_b3a6bd366c66":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","daemonization","background task scheduling","bash automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented a single Bash daemon script to replace multiple fragmented cron scripts.","Uses a 30-second loop to dispatch jobs at configurable cadences (30s, 60s, 5m, daily).","Jobs include live match sync, AI duel resolution, data pipeline refreshes, and daily prediction generation.","Includes built-in server health check via /api/debug/ping and log management."],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvqsryz_b3a6bd366c66","importance":7,"narrative":"Consolidated the project's background job management into a single, maintainable Bash orchestrator. This script improves reliability by running as a long-lived process with a supervised tick mechanism, replacing previous ad-hoc cron jobs.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"scripts/cron/tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:50:32.578Z","ti