uel resolution, and AI predictions.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Transitioned from live-match-cron.sh to a self-healing tick.sh supervisor","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:50:59.866Z","title":"Update setup-cron.sh to manage unified tick.sh orchestrator","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvqtjla_8e9757d84b17":{"concepts":["cron maintenance","bash automation","syntax validation","POSIX file permissions"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Removed deprecated files: scripts/cron/live-match-cron.sh and scripts/cron/update-5min.sh","Applied executable permissions to scripts/cron/tick.sh","Verified syntax of tick.sh and scripts/setup/setup-cron.sh using bash -n","Confirmed only tick.sh remains in scripts/cron/"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh","scripts/setup/setup-cron.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvqtjla_8e9757d84b17","importance":5,"narrative":"Performed maintenance on the cron infrastructure by removing legacy tasks and finalizing the tick.sh automation script. Syntax checks were successfully performed on all modified or critical cron-related scripts to ensure deployment stability.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Refactoring cron directory structure","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:51:08.373Z","title":"Cleanup and validation of cron scripts","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvqu03l_53fbd11a2b34":{"concepts":["shell scripting","timeout mechanism","log redirection","smoke testing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Executed scripts/cron/tick.sh with a 3-second timeout.","Captured output in /tmp/scoru-tick-test.log.","The command terminated with exit code 124 (timeout).","Log file was empty despite execution attempt."],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvqu03l_53fbd11a2b34","importance":4,"narrative":"Performed a smoke test on the tick.sh script by running it under a short timeout to observe behavior and logging. The process correctly exited with code 124, but the resulting log file was empty, indicating a potential issue with output redirection or script execution flow.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Verifying script behavior under timeout constraint","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:51:29.767Z","title":"Smoke test cron/tick.sh execution","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvquc7s_13413a03e2d4":{"concepts":["shell environment","process management","cron automation","linux utilities"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The command `timeout` is unavailable in the current shell environment.","Script `scripts/cron/tick.sh` was not executed due to command absence.","Exit status 0 was returned by the shell wrapper despite the missing binary."],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvquc7s_13413a03e2d4","importance":4,"narrative":"An attempt to execute a cron script with a timeout constraint failed because the `timeout` utility is not installed in the target environment. This necessitates an alternative approach for process execution management within the current shell.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Environment compatibility check for cron task","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:51:45.471Z","title":"Attempted execution of tick script via timeout","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvqulwz_58c69afaf62c":{"concepts":["background process","nohup","process management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Process started with PID 2133","Log output redirected to /tmp/tt.log via SCORU_LOG","Execution performed via nohup and background operator"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh","/tmp/tt.log"],"id":"obs_mpvqulwz_58c69afaf62c","importance":5,"narrative":"The tick.sh script was initiated as a background process to enable persistent execution. The output is being captured in /tmp/tt.log to monitor the background task status.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Execution of cron tick script detached from shell","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:51:58.040Z","title":"Start tick.sh background process","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvquq5i_37f5365c1fa7":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","process management","system monitoring"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Orchestrator started at 2026-06-02 00:51:58","Tick interval set to 30 seconds","Target server address: http://localhost:4321"],"files":["/tmp/tt.log","scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvquq5i_37f5365c1fa7","importance":4,"narrative":"The bash command successfully waited for the orchestrator to generate a log file, killed the background process, and retrieved the initialization log. The output confirms the SCORU cron orchestrator is active and correctly configured to poll the local server endpoint.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Observed tick log output from cron orchestrator","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:52:03.532Z","title":"Verification of SCORU cron orchestrator execution","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvqv0bs_5d9cc035c33c":{"concepts":["process management","cron automation","bash scripting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Attempted to kill process matching 'scripts/cron/tick.sh'","Implemented 1-second delay before verification","Process successfully terminated"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvqv0bs_5d9cc035c33c","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent executed a cleanup command to ensure that 'scripts/cron/tick.sh' is not currently active. Verification via pgrep confirmed the process was successfully terminated.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Verified cessation of scripts/cron/tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:52:16.715Z","title":"Ensure cron process termination","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr1i85_393a1f19646b":{"concepts":["Crontab scheduling","API rate limiting","Conditional automation","Resource optimization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Crontab task should check for active matches before proceeding with full API data ingestion.","Logic requires a pre-check script to inspect if matches exist before polling the primary endpoint.","Conditional execution avoids unnecessary rate-limiting and reduces compute cost."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvr1i85_393a1f19646b","importance":5,"narrative":"The user is planning to automate a livescore scraper via crontab and requested a strategy to minimize unnecessary API requests. I recommended implementing a conditional check that verifies the presence of active matches before fetching detailed event data.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Optimizing API usage for live sports tracking","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:57:19.846Z","title":"Crontab automation strategy for Livescore API","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvr2axb_81b71c942373":{"concepts":["background job","data synchronization","state machine","API integration"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Status mapping function `mapStatus` handles soccer match states: finished, scheduled, live, postponed, cancelled.","Match selection window queries DB for matches between 4h ago and 2h ahead with status 'live' or 'scheduled'.","Live matches are cross-referenced with Livescore API using the match eventDate.","Auto-closure logic: live matches with no feed entry older than 3.5 hours are candidates for closure.","State transition protection: matches that have started are prevented from downgrading back to 'scheduled'."],"files":["src/pages/api/jobs/live-matches.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvr2axb_81b71c942373","importance":4,"narrative":"Inspected the job logic for synchronizing live soccer matches. The code confirms a time-window-based approach for identifying active candidates and uses status mapping to prevent invalid state transitions once a match has started.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Reviewing status mapping and update logic in live-matches.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:57:57.031Z","title":"Inspect live-matches job logic","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvr36ei_0862093174b0":{"concepts":["Bash scripting","cron orchestration","API efficiency","short-circuit evaluation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Modified job_live function in scripts/cron/tick.sh","Added parsing of potentialMatches field from /api/jobs/live-matches response","If potentialMatches is 0, the script now skips enhancement and SSE notification steps","Reduces network overhead during periods with no active matches"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr36ei_0862093174b0","importance":5,"narrative":"The cron tick script was performing unnecessary API calls and data processing for live matches even when no matches were currently occurring. By checking the potentialMatches count from the status endpoint, the script can now short-circuit the execution, saving system resources and reducing server noise.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Added conditional logic to skip live processing when no matches are active","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:58:37.840Z","title":"Optimize cron job_live for idle detection","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvr3azc_5c992fc05877":{"concepts":["cron job","process management","shell scripting","automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Shell syntax for scripts/cron/tick.sh is valid","Crontab entry includes pgrep lock check to prevent overlapping executions","Logs are redirected to $HOME/scoru-cron.log","Uses nohup and background execution for continuous background processing"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr3azc_5c992fc05877","importance":5,"narrative":"The script syntax was validated using bash -n to ensure no parsing errors. A robust crontab entry was generated, incorporating a pgrep check to ensure only one instance of the tick script runs at any time, which is essential for stable background task orchestration.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Verified scripts/cron/tick.sh syntax and prepared crontab entry","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:58:43.774Z","title":"Validate cron script and generate deployment line","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr44lk_b69943109d29":{"concepts":["bash","process synchronization","cron orchestration","PID file"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added lock file management via $SCORU_PID env var (default: ~/.scoru-tick.pid).","Implemented a bash guard that checks for existing process using kill -0.","Added an EXIT/INT/TERM trap to ensure the PID file is removed on shutdown."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr44lk_b69943109d29","importance":6,"narrative":"To prevent race conditions and overlapping execution of the cron orchestrator, I added a PID file guard to tick.sh. This ensures only one instance of the script runs at a time by verifying the liveness of the process ID recorded in the lock file.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Implementing PID file guard for tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:59:22.159Z","title":"Add single-instance locking to cron orchestrator","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvr4cc0_b532ffbc557c":{"concepts":["cron","process supervision","shell scripting","PID file management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Replaced pgrep-based process tracking with PID file checking (kill -0) in setup-cron.sh.","Previous implementation using pgrep had a flaw where it matched its own crontab entry, causing restart loops or process detection issues.","The supervisor now expects a PID file at $HOME/.scoru-tick.pid."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/setup/setup-cron.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr4cc0_b532ffbc557c","importance":6,"narrative":"The cron orchestrator setup was updated to use a more robust process monitoring method. By switching from pgrep to checking the process status via a PID file, the script prevents accidental self-matching and ensures the orchestrator (tick.sh) is accurately monitored.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Replacing unreliable pgrep match with PID file validation in setup-cron.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:59:32.180Z","title":"Update crontab supervisor to use PID file instead of pgrep","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvr4msb_02764fe2b4d5":{"concepts":["process locking","PID file management","bash shell scripting","concurrency control"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Validated syntax for tick.sh and setup-cron.sh using bash -n","Confirmed tick.sh successfully detects existing process via /tmp/.tickpid","Identified failure to clean up /tmp/.tickpid after pkill"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh","scripts/setup/setup-cron.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr4msb_02764fe2b4d5","importance":5,"narrative":"Performed a smoke test on the cron tick script to verify that the single-instance locking mechanism functions correctly. While the locking logic itself works, the test revealed that the PID file persists after the process is killed, indicating a lack of proper cleanup handling.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Validation of PID file locking logic in tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T21:59:45.730Z","title":"Verify cron tick single-instance locking","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr5avp_d3585a83b35e":{"concepts":["process management","cron automation","PID file management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["pkill failed to terminate scripts/cron/tick.sh as confirmed by subsequent pgrep output","The target script is still running","Removed local PID file at $HOME/.scoru-tick.pid"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr5avp_d3585a83b35e","importance":5,"narrative":"An attempt to stop the tick.sh cron process was performed, but the process remains active despite the command execution. The PID file was removed as a precautionary measure, but manual intervention or a more forceful termination may be required.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Force stop scripts/cron/tick.sh and cleanup","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:00:16.953Z","title":"Attempt to terminate tick script","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr5iig_1771e7d5b06a":{"concepts":["process management","cron job","PID file cleanup","POSIX signals"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Process 2872 (scripts/cron/tick.sh) was identified and killed","SIGKILL (-9) was used to ensure process termination","Stale PID file .scoru-tick.pid was removed"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh","$HOME/.scoru-tick.pid"],"id":"obs_mpvr5iig_1771e7d5b06a","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent force-terminated a background cron script to clear the environment or reset state. It verified successful termination and cleaned up the associated PID file to prevent stale process errors.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Terminate scripts/cron/tick.sh and cleanup PID","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:00:26.845Z","title":"Force kill tick process","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr5w83_a4d59a1dc2c8":{"concepts":["bash","signal handling","process orchestration","mutex pattern"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Modified trap command to separate EXIT cleanup from INT/TERM signal cleanup","Explicitly added exit 0 to the INT/TERM signal handler to prevent accidental script resumption"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr5w83_a4d59a1dc2c8","importance":4,"narrative":"The script's process management was updated to ensure robust lock file removal. By decoupling the traps, the system now ensures the lock file is removed regardless of whether the script finishes naturally or is killed via interrupt signals.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Decoupling EXIT from signal handling for lock file cleanup","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:00:44.615Z","title":"Update trap handling in tick.sh","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvr64ec_76fc6e54a225":{"concepts":["process management","signal handling","bash automation","PID file management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Script scripts/cron/tick.sh has valid bash syntax","The script successfully handles SIGTERM by stopping execution","The script correctly removes its PID file (/tmp/.tp2) upon exit","Process verified to be terminated via pgrep check"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr64ec_76fc6e54a225","importance":5,"narrative":"Verified the termination logic of the cron script to ensure it does not leave orphaned processes or stale PID files. The test confirms that the script shuts down cleanly upon receiving a TERM signal and handles its temporary file cleanup correctly.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Testing graceful shutdown and PID file cleanup for scripts/cron/tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:00:55.210Z","title":"Verification of script lifecycle management","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvr89pz_0a95ebd956e0":{"concepts":["production readiness","shell scripting","deployment stability"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User is evaluating the reliability of tick.sh for production environments.","The script currently lacks explicit production-grade validation or error handling documentation."],"files":["tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvr89pz_0a95ebd956e0","importance":5,"narrative":"The user is concerned about the production stability of the tick.sh script. This inquiry necessitates a review of the script's robustness, including dependency management, environment variables, and fail-safe mechanisms.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"User verifying deployment reliability for shell script","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:02:35.421Z","title":"Inquiry regarding production readiness of tick.sh","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpvra4ln_87ff65506b99":{"concepts":["Coolify","Systemd","VPS deployment","Linux server management"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Production environment confirmed as Coolify running on a Linux VPS.","Systemd unit deployment strategy will be prioritized over containerized workers."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvra4ln_87ff65506b99","importance":6,"narrative":"The user clarified that the production hosting will be managed via Coolify on a Linux server. This informs the deployment strategy, shifting focus from serverless or container-specific workflows to native systemd service management for stability and persistence.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Target platform: Coolify / Linux VPS","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:04:02.094Z","title":"Production environment configuration established","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvrbrai_2f058385445d":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","OpenRouter API","Sports Analytics Pipeline","LLM structured output"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Script handles comprehensive sports predictions (1X2, score, O/U 2.5, BTTS, first goalscorer).","Uses Drizzle ORM and Postgres for database interaction.","Relies on OpenRouter API for model inference.","Stores results in ai_comprehensive_predictions table.","Supports date-specific execution via CLI argument."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/ai/generate-comprehensive.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrbrai_2f058385445d","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent read the generation script to understand how AI predictions are computed and stored. This script acts as the primary pipeline for populating the comprehensive predictions table used by the match interface.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Examining generate-comprehensive.ts script logic","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:05:18.160Z","title":"Read AI prediction generation script","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvrbvmh_3d3025f96d36":{"concepts":["TypeScript interfaces","LLM structured output","API retry strategy","Schema validation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The script defines a 'Comprehensive' interface for sports prediction data schema.","Includes a 'validate' function enforcing output strictness for 5 required fields.","Uses 'ask' and 'askOnce' functions to interface with an LLM API, including retry logic with backoff.","Main entry point fetches match data for a specific date from a database via drizzle/sql."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/ai/generate-comprehensive.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrbvmh_3d3025f96d36","importance":5,"narrative":"I reviewed the comprehensive prediction generation script to understand how it interfaces with LLMs to produce structured betting predictions. The code enforces strict JSON schema validation and handles API resilience through a retry mechanism with incremental backoff.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Examining generate-comprehensive.ts logic and validation","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:05:23.772Z","title":"Read AI generation script for match predictions","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvrctfu_189007ea0e4a":{"concepts":["Drizzle ORM","OpenRouter API","Structured JSON output","Prediction modeling"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented comprehensive prediction generator using OpenRouter API.","Supports 1X2, exact score, over/under, BTTS, and first goalscorer fields.","Includes validation logic for AI-generated JSON responses.","Designed for reuse by both CLI scripts and API endpoints."],"files":["src/lib/server/ai-predict.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrctfu_189007ea0e4a","importance":7,"narrative":"Created a centralized module for generating sports betting predictions via AI models. This ensures consistent logic for both batch processing (CLI) and on-demand generation (API) while standardizing the output structure and validation schema.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"src/lib/server/ai-predict.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:06:07.596Z","title":"Created AI prediction engine module","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrd2bm_45e66be8c76c":{"concepts":["DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)","CLI automation","Code consolidation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Replaced inline database and AI logic with import from src/lib/server/ai-predict.ts","Updated CLI script to act as a thin wrapper for generateDailyPredictions","CLI commands updated to npm run ai:predict","Removed local dependencies on drizzle-orm, postgres, and schema definitions from the script"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/ai/generate-comprehensive.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrd2bm_45e66be8c76c","importance":5,"narrative":"The logic for generating comprehensive AI predictions was previously duplicated between the CLI script and the server endpoint. By centralizing this logic into ai-predict.ts, maintenance is improved and both environments remain in sync.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Consolidated generate-comprehensive.ts with server logic","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:06:19.110Z","title":"Refactor CLI script to use shared prediction logic","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvrd99h_0ca857e13e61":{"concepts":["Astro API Routes","Serverless architecture","Idempotency","Automation scheduling"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented POST endpoint at /api/ai/generate-daily","Uses generateDailyPredictions utility for logic","Handles optional date input in YYYY-MM-DD format","Designed for non-interactive execution (cron jobs, serverless)"],"files":["src/pages/api/ai/generate-daily.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrd99h_0ca857e13e61","importance":6,"narrative":"Created a new Astro API endpoint to trigger AI prediction generation. This endpoint is designed to be idempotent and runtime-agnostic, making it suitable for automated daily scheduling tasks like Coolify crons or serverless environments.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"src/pages/api/ai/generate-daily.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:06:28.104Z","title":"Created serverless API endpoint for AI predictions","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrdgmh_723ba2ea6e81":{"concepts":["bash scripting","cron orchestration","API automation","process optimization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Replaced 'npm run ai:predict' execution with a direct curl POST to '/api/ai/generate-daily'.","Added manual parsing of JSON response to extract 'matches' count using grep and cut.","Included fallback logic to report 0 matches if parsing fails or result is empty.","Eliminated dependency on 'tsx' and local Node.js environment overhead for this specific cron job."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrdgmh_723ba2ea6e81","importance":5,"narrative":"The 'job_predict' function in the cron orchestrator was updated to invoke the AI prediction endpoint directly via HTTP. This reduces latency and resource usage by avoiding a full Node.js process startup for each execution, while improving observability by logging the specific number of matches processed.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Replacing npm script execution with curl/POST call","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:06:37.647Z","title":"Refactor job_predict in tick.sh to use direct HTTP API","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvrdvbr_2dc2e071a9cd":{"concepts":["API testing","Cron job","TypeScript typecheck","CLI automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["CLI command `npm run ai:predict` for 2020-01-01 returns 0 matches.","Endpoint `/api/ai/generate-daily` confirms success but returns 0 matches for 2020-01-01.","`src/lib/server/ai-predict.ts` passed basic TypeScript type checking.","`scripts/cron/tick.sh` passed bash syntax validation."],"files":["src/lib/server/ai-predict.ts","scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrdvbr_2dc2e071a9cd","importance":4,"narrative":"Validated the AI prediction pipeline by testing both the CLI and API endpoint against a past date, confirming they handle empty result sets gracefully. Also verified the structural integrity of the TS prediction module and the cron trigger script.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Validating CLI, endpoint, and script syntax for past date","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:06:56.701Z","title":"Verification of AI prediction logic and scripts","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvrf282_e8faebe26aa3":{"concepts":["Astro API Routes","Cron Job Orchestration","Data Pipeline Enhancement","Server-Sent Events"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Endpoint fetches current match status from /api/jobs/live-matches","Conditional execution: triggers /api/data-pipeline/enhance-live only if potential matches > 0","Triggers /api/live/events upon successful enhancement","Uses internal fetch calls to trigger secondary API routes"],"files":["src/pages/api/cron/live-tick.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrf282_e8faebe26aa3","importance":6,"narrative":"Created a new cron-triggered API route to manage the lifecycle of live match updates. This endpoint centralizes logic to ensure data enhancement and SSE event notification only occur when active matches exist, minimizing unnecessary processing overhead.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Implemented /api/cron/live-tick","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:07:52.295Z","title":"Created Cron Job API endpoint for live match processing","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrf9sf_e016e7c0a316":{"concepts":["API Orchestration","Cron Job","Data Pipeline","Astro API Routes"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Created file at src/pages/api/cron/refresh.ts","Endpoint triggers a sequence of internal API calls: pull-by-date, assign-teams, assign-competitions, and assign-matches","Uses local fetch calls to trigger modular pipeline steps","Designed to pull fixture data for a 2-day window (today + tomorrow)"],"files":["src/pages/api/cron/refresh.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrf9sf_e016e7c0a316","importance":6,"narrative":"This endpoint serves as a controller for the data pipeline, allowing external schedulers to trigger a full refresh of fixture data. It orchestrates multiple assignment tasks to ensure that teams, competitions, and matches are synchronized after pulling new data.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Implemented /api/cron/refresh for automated data orchestration","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:08:02.099Z","title":"Created Cron Refresh API endpoint","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrfkwr_16c641cf2d89":{"concepts":["cron automation","orchestration pattern","API-driven cron","shell script optimization"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Replaced manual multi-step logic in job_live with a single call to /api/cron/live-tick.","Replaced bulk assignment/pull logic in job_refresh with a single call to /api/cron/refresh.","Reduced bash script complexity by offloading orchestration responsibility to the application server."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrfkwr_16c641cf2d89","importance":6,"narrative":"The cron orchestration script was simplified to reduce bash-side logic, delegating orchestrating tasks (like multi-endpoint data pipeline refreshing) to dedicated API endpoints on the server. This reduces brittle shell parsing and improves maintainability of the background job cadence.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Simplified job_live and job_refresh logic by delegating to server-side endpoints","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:08:16.512Z","title":"Refactor cron tick.sh to use single-endpoint triggers","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvrfsl8_9a81f93d88c0":{"concepts":["bash","shell script optimization","environment variable cleanup"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Removed PROJECT_DIR definition from /Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh","PROJECT_DIR was previously derived using BASH_SOURCE path resolution","The variable was not utilized in the script logic"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrfsl8_9a81f93d88c0","importance":4,"narrative":"The PROJECT_DIR variable was removed from the initialization block of the cron orchestrator script because it served no functional purpose. This simplifies the configuration header and reduces unnecessary environment overhead for the process.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Clean up unused environment variable definition in bash script","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:08:26.466Z","title":"Remove PROJECT_DIR from tick.sh","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvrfynw_ea111ea86436":{"concepts":["bash","cron orchestration","refactoring"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Removed 'postj' function from /Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh","'postj' was a utility for JSON POST requests, currently unused by defined job functions"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrfynw_ea111ea86436","importance":3,"narrative":"The 'postj' helper function was removed to reduce clutter in the cron orchestrator script. No job functions were currently utilizing this endpoint helper, so its removal simplifies the script's core API interaction layer.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Cleaned up cron script dependencies","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:08:34.336Z","title":"Remove unused postj helper from tick.sh","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvrgrc6_9e098ec62bfb":{"concepts":["API testing","cron jobs","shell script validation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["live-tick endpoint returned success with 1 potential item","refresh endpoint executed successfully for date 2026-06-01","scripts/cron/tick.sh passed bash syntax check (-n)"],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrgrc6_9e098ec62bfb","importance":4,"narrative":"Performed a diagnostic check on the cron infrastructure by triggering live-tick and refresh endpoints. Additionally, verified that the cron tick script is syntactically valid before further automation or scheduling.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Validating API responses and shell script integrity","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:09:11.488Z","title":"Verification of cron endpoints and script syntax","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvrho47_d33e87c5d194":{"concepts":["Coolify","Cron","Infrastructure as Code","Deployment automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Production cron jobs migrated to Coolify Scheduled Tasks calling HTTP endpoints.","tick.sh script reserved exclusively for local development.","Live sync task implements 30s cadence via 'sleep 30' inside a 1-minute cron job.","Commands executed via curl against localhost:$PORT within the application container."],"files":["scripts/cron/COOLIFY.md"],"id":"obs_mpvrho47_d33e87c5d194","importance":5,"narrative":"Created documentation detailing how to configure cron jobs in Coolify using HTTP endpoints instead of external shell scripts. This ensures better observability through the Coolify UI and eliminates runtime dependency on tsx/npm in production.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Transitioning from local shell scripts to HTTP endpoint-based tasks","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:09:53.978Z","title":"Documentation for Coolify Cron setup","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrrbt2_6e0d79593ee0":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","API design","task scheduling"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Orchestrator currently requires 4 separate cron jobs.","Requirement is to consolidate into a single cron job that triggers all sub-tasks.","Production environment requires HTTP GET for cron triggers instead of POST."],"files":["src/orchestrator.ts","package.json"],"id":"obs_mpvrrbt2_6e0d79593ee0","importance":7,"narrative":"The user identified a design flaw where the orchestrator was underutilized, requiring manual setup of multiple cron jobs. I need to consolidate these into a single entry point and update all internal triggers to use GET requests to ensure production compatibility.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Centralizing cron execution in Orchestrator","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:17:24.587Z","title":"Refactor Orchestrator Logic for Cron Consolidation","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvrtq4v_6949d3a58604":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","event loop delegation","Astro API routes","idempotent task scheduling"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Endpoint handles multi-cadence job triggering via a single cron hook.","Uses nested setTimeouts for sub-minute task execution.","Separates awaited tasks (live sync, resolution) from fire-and-forget tasks (refresh, AI generation).","Daily AI generation threshold is configurable via SCORU_PREDICT_HOUR env var."],"files":["src/pages/api/cron/tick.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvrtq4v_6949d3a58604","importance":8,"narrative":"Created a centralized server-side orchestrator to manage multiple scheduled tasks from a single cron heartbeat. This pattern allows for varied execution cadences (every minute, 5 minutes, daily) while keeping the API response fast by decoupling execution using non-awaited fetch calls.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Implemented src/pages/api/cron/tick.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:19:16.467Z","title":"Created central cron orchestrator endpoint","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrtvy5_c62a6463c981":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","shell scripting","background job scheduling","single-instance lock"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Script implements a 30-second polling loop for background jobs.","Jobs include live sync (30s), duel resolution (60s), data refresh (5m), and daily AI predictions (at configured hour).","Includes single-instance locking mechanism using PID file.","Environment variables: SCORU_URL (default localhost:4321), SCORU_LOG, SCORU_PREDICT_HOUR (default 03)."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvrtvy5_c62a6463c981","importance":5,"narrative":"The script acts as the centralized cron supervisor for the SCORU platform, replacing multiple legacy scripts with a single persistent process. It relies on internal loop counters and simple date comparisons to trigger job execution against specific API endpoints.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Analysis of scripts/cron/tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:19:24.001Z","title":"Read SCORU unified cron orchestrator script","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvru6jy_ab3ab8983145":{"concepts":["Cron orchestration","DevOps","HTTP polling","Process management","Coolify"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The script now acts as a local developer convenience tool rather than a complex multi-cadence runner.","Production scheduling is now offloaded to a Coolify task hitting GET /api/cron/tick.","Replaced custom logic with a simple 60s curl loop to the /api/cron/tick endpoint.","Maintained single-instance process locking using PID files."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvru6jy_ab3ab8983145","importance":5,"narrative":"The previous cron orchestration script was overly complex, attempting to manage multiple cadences locally. I refactored it to simply mirror the production environment's strategy: a single recurring HTTP call to the server-side orchestrator. This simplifies the development loop and aligns it with the production Coolify deployment pattern.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Refactored scripts/cron/tick.sh to mirror production Coolify behavior","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:19:37.748Z","title":"Replaced complex local cron loop with simple HTTP ping runner","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvrum5o_7467c5817cc8":{"concepts":["Coolify deployment","Cron orchestration","Server-side task scheduling","Fire-and-forget patterns"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Transitioned from multiple scheduled tasks to a single cron job hitting /api/cron/tick per minute","Centralized scheduling logic server-side to handle live sync, duel resolution, data refresh, and AI generation","Tick endpoint uses GET for simplicity and compatibility with standard crons","Node process remains persistent in Coolify to allow fire-and-forget background jobs"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/COOLIFY.md"],"id":"obs_mpvrum5o_7467c5817cc8","importance":7,"narrative":"Simplified the infrastructure by moving cron orchestration from container-level scheduled tasks to a single endpoint trigger. This approach uses a persistent Node process to handle asynchronous tasks reliably after the initial HTTP request returns, significantly reducing complexity in Coolify's task management.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Centralizing job orchestration via GET /api/cron/tick","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:19:57.970Z","title":"Update Coolify production cron strategy","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpvruvxl_f03c67d0e033":{"concepts":["API validation","cron job orchestration","shell script linting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["/api/cron/tick successfully executed, returning success status and trigger actions.","scripts/cron/tick.sh passed syntax check (bash -n).","src/pages/api/cron/tick.ts is confirmed as the unique GET endpoint for external cron hits."],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh","src/pages/api/cron/tick.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvruvxl_f03c67d0e033","importance":4,"narrative":"The environment was validated by triggering the cron endpoint via curl and checking script syntax. The results confirm the API endpoint is functioning and the corresponding helper script is syntactically correct.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Validating /api/cron/tick and scripts/cron/tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:20:10.638Z","title":"Verification of API Cron Endpoint and Script Syntax","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvryboh_519ba4a8518c":{"concepts":["CRON job","task scheduling","real-time synchronization"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User identified potential discrepancy in live data synchronization interval.","Current expectation is a 30-second CRON interval instead of the existing 1-minute frequency."],"files":["not_specified"],"id":"obs_mpvryboh_519ba4a8518c","importance":5,"narrative":"The user questioned the current execution frequency of the live synchronization task, suggesting it should be updated to 30 seconds to maintain real-time accuracy. This indicates a requirement to investigate and modify the scheduling configuration for the background process responsible for live updates.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Refining live synchronization interval","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:22:50.995Z","title":"CRON execution frequency adjustment","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvs09ha_37b855567813":{"concepts":["cron orchestration","throttling","API automation","Astro API Routes"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented time-based throttling logic using module-level state variables.","Supported ~30s execution using a double-curl shell command in Coolify.","Maintained tiered cadence: real-time (live/resolve), 5-min (refresh), and daily (AI)."],"files":["src/pages/api/cron/tick.ts"],"id":"obs_mpvs09ha_37b855567813","importance":6,"narrative":"The cron orchestrator was updated to allow for more frequent execution (30s intervals) without overloading system resources. By implementing local state throttling, the endpoint can now be called as often as desired while ensuring expensive tasks like data refresh and AI generation only trigger on their configured schedule.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Updated /api/cron/tick to handle 30s-interval polling","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:24:21.474Z","title":"Refactor cron orchestrator to support sub-minute execution","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvs0j03_579b2776597a":{"concepts":["cron automation","polling loop","shell scripting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Polling frequency increased from 60 seconds to 30 seconds.","Target endpoint: /api/cron/tick.","Modification applied to the local development script."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvs0j03_579b2776597a","importance":4,"narrative":"The cron runner loop in scripts/cron/tick.sh was modified to increase the execution frequency by reducing the sleep interval from 60 to 30 seconds. This ensures the local development environment triggers the cron tasks more frequently to match testing requirements.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Change tick interval from 60s to 30s in tick.sh","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:24:33.819Z","title":"Update cron runner polling interval","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvs0yr5_475497059358":{"concepts":["cron job scheduling","Coolify deployment","polling mechanism","idempotent tasks"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Updated Coolify Scheduled Task command to use `sh -c 'curl ...; sleep 30; curl ...'` to achieve 30-second interval polling.","Refined documentation to clarify that `/api/cron/tick` uses internal throttling/logic to handle job frequency (live sync, duel resolution, date refresh, AI generation).","The command is executed as a GET request via crontab-like frequency (1 minute interval)."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/scripts/cron/COOLIFY.md"],"id":"obs_mpvs0yr5_475497059358","importance":5,"narrative":"Updated the technical documentation in COOLIFY.md to reflect the correct implementation for achieving sub-minute cron resolution on Coolify. By wrapping the curl calls in an sh -c command with a sleep interval, the system successfully hits the heartbeat endpoint twice per minute, ensuring live data freshness.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Clarifying 30s interval execution via sh -c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:24:54.233Z","title":"Update Coolify cron documentation","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpvs16yr_6c67f33d7576":{"concepts":["API throttling","Cron job","Task scheduling","Bash scripting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["First API call executed 'live', 'resolve', and 'refresh' tasks.","Second API call (2 seconds later) executed only 'live' and 'resolve', confirming the 'refresh' task is successfully throttled.","scripts/cron/tick.sh passed syntax check (bash -n)."],"files":["scripts/cron/tick.sh"],"id":"obs_mpvs16yr_6c67f33d7576","importance":5,"narrative":"The cron tick API was tested to confirm that the task throttle prevents the 'refresh' task from running within a short time window. The test successfully demonstrated that the 'refresh' task is excluded on subsequent calls, validating the throttle logic and ensuring the syntax of the underlying script is correct.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Testing API throttle behavior and script syntax","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:25:04.873Z","title":"Verify cron tick throttle logic","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpvs6imf_00d95197cb48":{"concepts":["arbitrage betting","expected value","market efficiency","hedging"],"confidence":1,"facts":["User is investigating if betting against multiple AI entities allows for guaranteed arbitrage.","The core question concerns whether covering all possible outcomes across AI predictions results in a risk-free profit.","General betting theory suggests that arbitrage requires odds mismatches, which automated AI systems would likely normalize."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvs6imf_00d95197cb48","importance":3,"narrative":"The user is questioning the feasibility of an arbitrage strategy involving multiple AI agents. This is fundamentally limited by the inherent \"vig\" or house edge in betting markets, which ensures that covering all outcomes usually results in a net loss regardless of the entity generating the predictions.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Analysis of betting mechanics and hedging strategies","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:29:13.261Z","title":"Betting logic inquiry: Arbitrage against AI-managed outcomes","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpvsee55_4f6e88d5acb4":{"concepts":["subagent orchestration","process lifecycle"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Subagent execution stopped at 2026-06-01T22:35:20.701Z","Signal received: subagent_stop"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvsee55_4f6e88d5acb4","importance":3,"narrative":"The active subagent has terminated its execution process. This indicates the completion of its assigned sub-task or an interruption of the delegated workflow.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Completion of subagent task","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:35:20.701Z","title":"Subagent process termination","type":"subagent"},"obs_mpvseec0_e1bd97819d71":{"concepts":["Game Economy","Virtual Currency","Monetization Strategy","User Retention","Gamification"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Proposed sign-up bonus of 1,000 units of virtual currency.","Betting mechanism planned for user engagement and currency replenishment.","Future roadmap includes fiat currency conversion and direct purchase of virtual assets.","Considering branding the currency as a proprietary token rather than generic \"crystals\"."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvseec0_e1bd97819d71","importance":8,"narrative":"The user wants to gamify the platform by introducing a virtual currency system that supports betting, sign-up bonuses, and future monetization. We discussed the necessity of replenishment loops for users who lose their initial balance and the long-term feasibility of a custom token economy.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Strategic planning for user retention and monetization mechanics","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:35:20.949Z","title":"Economy Design: Virtual Currency and Betting System","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvslnl1_eddb58cd7db0":{"concepts":["P2P economy","Liquidity management","Gaming economy","Escrow systems"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The user is investigating the mechanism for fund withdrawal/value realization in a P2P duel system.","The query specifically targets scenarios where traditional \"cash-out\" mechanisms are bypassed.","The goal is to understand how winners in competitive duels access their winnings without direct cash-out flow."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvslnl1_eddb58cd7db0","importance":4,"narrative":"The user is asking about the internal economic model of a P2P gaming platform, specifically focusing on how winners collect rewards without a standard cash-out process. This suggests interest in alternative liquidity methods, such as in-game credit systems, P2P transfers, or external wallet integration.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"User query regarding value extraction in user-vs-user duels","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:40:59.527Z","title":"Inquiry on P2P gaming economy and non-cashout mechanics","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpvsupex_6438dcbd82ae":{"concepts":["In-game economy","Gambling law","Virtual currency regulation","Skill-based gaming"],"confidence":1,"facts":["User proposes a tournament-based economy using virtual \"crystals\".","Proposed entry fee is 20,000 crystals, with a first-place prize of 100,000 crystals.","Primary concern is avoiding legal classification as gambling."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvsupex_6438dcbd82ae","importance":7,"narrative":"The user is exploring the legal viability of a skill-based tournament system using virtual currency. The core challenge is navigating the regulatory definition of gambling, which typically requires a bet of value, a game of chance, and a prize of monetary value.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Evaluating potential gambling classification for tournament prize systems","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:48:01.806Z","title":"Legal Analysis of In-Game Economy and Prize Pools","type":"decision"},"obs_mpvt3iyo_6f71e46b5c32":{"concepts":["UX design","feature validation","gamification","user engagement"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User questions the necessity of skins/cosmetics in the app.","User notes that app usage patterns differ from gaming, where cosmetics are persistent."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpvt3iyo_6f71e46b5c32","importance":4,"narrative":"The user expressed skepticism regarding the implementation of a skin or cosmetic system, arguing that the application's context does not support the same engagement model as video games. This feedback challenges the premise of cosmetic features and suggests a need to rethink user motivation for such items.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Discussion regarding the relevance of cosmetic items in the current application context","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:54:53.326Z","title":"User inquiry on feature utility for skin system","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpvt8r19_1ca3b0d316be":{"concepts":["file system navigation","task management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Project root contains a /tasks directory with individual task text files","Master task registry found at /tasks/tasks.json (158KB)","Found .taskmasterconfig in project root","No .taskmaster directory exists"],"files":["/tasks/tasks.json",".taskmasterconfig"],"id":"obs_mpvt8r19_1ca3b0d316be","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent explored the directory structure to locate task-tracking information. It confirmed that tasks are managed within a /tasks folder containing individual text files and a centralized tasks.json manifest.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Identified task repository and configuration files","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:58:57.091Z","title":"Directory listing and task discovery","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpvt8w8y_598045a63b9f":{"concepts":["task tracking","data serialization","JSON parsing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Successfully parsed tasks/tasks.json using a custom Node.js script.","Majority of project tasks (1-18) are marked as 'done'.","Tasks 14, 15, and 16 contain subtasks with 'completed' status but missing titles."],"files":["tasks/tasks.json"],"id":"obs_mpvt8w8y_598045a63b9f","importance":3,"narrative":"Executed a script to aggregate and display all task statuses from the project configuration file. The output confirms that the core project features—including authentication, data models, AI prediction integration, and the 'Parte-n Parte' challenge system—are essentially marked as complete, though some subtask metadata remains incomplete.","sessionId":"945fa316-ea0b-42eb-ad6e-a5b5d9559fb7","subtitle":"Verified completion status via tasks.json script","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:59:03.849Z","title":"Audit current project task status","type":"task"},"obs_mpvt95z7_15f82b31389d":{"concepts":["refactoring","Nano Stores","database schema design","state management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Task 22: Scripts folder reorganization requires new directory structure and package.json path updates.","Task 22 depends on Task 29 (Database Schema Cleanup).","Task 25: Develop team pages and stats system using Nano Stores for state management.","Task 25 involves database schema design for teams, players, and matches."],"files":["tasks/task_022.txt","tasks/task_025.txt","tasks/task_028.t